0302: call a host-memory command list (City Folk; generic)

GX_AURORA_CALL_HOST_DL (u64 pointer, u32 size): processes a command list in host memory in place.
For display lists recorded in Aurora's encoding that do not fit the game's buffer (Aurora's texture,
array and draw commands are longer than the console's): the game's buffer holds a 32-byte call to
the host copy, so the game keeps calling the list through its own buffer (port: hle_gx.cpp).

diff --git a/include/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.h b/include/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.h
index 20335be..ae8cdcd 100644
--- a/include/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.h
+++ b/include/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.h
@@ -174,6 +174,13 @@ extern "C" {
  */
 #define GX_AURORA_PROBE_TAG 0x0068
 
+/*
+ * 0302: call a host-memory command list: u64 pointer, u32 size (big-endian). For display lists
+ * recorded in Aurora's encoding that did not fit the game's buffer: the game's buffer then holds
+ * only this call, and the list itself lives in host memory (kept alive by the caller).
+ */
+#define GX_AURORA_CALL_HOST_DL 0x0069
+
 #define GX2_SET_POLYGON_OFFSET 0x1000
 
 
